# .dockerignore applies ONLY to its own build context directory.
# The context here is ./Backend, so this file must live here — a
# .dockerignore at the repo root is never read for this build.

# Host build output. obj/project.assets.json records Windows NuGet
# paths; copying it into a Linux image breaks `dotnet publish` with
# "Unable to find fallback package folder 'C:\Program Files...'".
**/bin
**/obj

# Editor / OS noise
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.user
**/*.suo


# Backups created before containerising
**/*.bak

# Local secrets are injected at runtime, never baked into an image
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/*.pfx

# NOTE: do NOT add 'Dockerfile' or '.dockerignore' here.
# Some builders (Render's, and BuildKit in certain configurations) resolve the
# Dockerfile THROUGH the filtered build context. Excluding it makes the build fail
# with 'failed to read dockerfile: no such file or directory' and a telltale
# 'transferring dockerfile: 2B'. Local `docker compose build` does NOT reproduce
# this, because Compose reads the Dockerfile from disk and sends it separately.
